": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170413 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/e3471526f4c71b2c4ee00117e125e179da01e6e2/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\nThe read tool failed on the directory itself with a confusing error (\"File not found\", then it suggested the same path). I'll list the directory with bash and run the tests.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nNow applying the fixes.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nAll 16 tests now pass when I run `python3 -m unittest`.\n\n**The three reads you asked for:**\n- **(a) Reading `catalog/` with the read tool failed.** It returned \"File not found\" and then suggested the exact same path. So it doesn't list directories, and the error message is misleading. I used `ls` instead: the folder has `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py` and `text.py`.\n- **(b) Offset 0, limit 5** returned lines 1\u20135 of `books.py`.\n- **(c) Offset 3, limit 5** returned lines 4\u20138, not 3\u20137, and only 5 lines. So the offset counts from 0 (offset 3 starts at the 4th line), which matches what (b) shows.\n\n**Fixes, all in `catalog/`; I didn't touch the tests:**\n- `books.py`: `parse_book` now turns the year into a number with `int(year)`. It was a string, which broke `age()`.\n- `factory.py`: added the missing `Emma` book, so the sample set has the three titles its docstring describes.\n- `fees.py`: the fee is now days late \u00d7 the daily fee. It was adding them.\n- `inventory.py`: `recent(n)` was returning one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n`, and an empty list when `n <= 0`.\n- `members.py`: `MAX_BORROWED` changed from 3 to 5, matching the policy comment above it.\n- `search.py`: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`); it now imports it from `catalog.text`.\n\nThe suite runs 16 tests now instead of 15 because `test_search` loads properly. Before, its two tests showed up as a single import error.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 69931, "requests_cache_write": 84668, "requests_cost_usd": 0.49526619999999993, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2893, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-read-edge:claude-opus-5-5:trial27", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 292, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T08:01:56.671299+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 35.244, "t_checker_s": 0.175, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-read-edge", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 2913, "tokens_cache_read": 69931, "tokens_cache_write": 84668, "tokens_fresh": 2895, "tokens_input_uncached": 20, "tokens_main_cache_read": 68899, "tokens_main_cache_write": 84668, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_output": 2879, "token